5. STUDENT APPROVAL SYSTEM

Implement a complete registration approval workflow.

When a student registers:
	1.	Create the student account in the database.
	2.	Assign the STUDENT role.
	3.	Set the account status to PENDING APPROVAL.
	4.	Display a clear pending approval message.
	5.	Prevent access to protected learning materials.
	6.	Display the registration request in the Super Admin dashboard.
	7.	Allow the Super Admin to approve or reject the registration.

After approval:
	•	Change the account status to APPROVED.
	•	Allow the student to log in and access the learning platform.
	•	Save the approval date and the administrator responsible for the action.

After rejection:
	•	Change the account status to REJECTED.
	•	Block access to protected content.
	•	Display an appropriate status message.

The Super Admin must also be able to suspend, deactivate, and restore accounts at any time.

Important security requirement

Account approval must be enforced by the backend.

Do not simply hide dashboard components or buttons from unapproved users.

Unapproved students must not be able to access protected information by:
	•	Entering a direct URL.
	•	Refreshing a protected page.
	•	Calling an API endpoint.
	•	Manipulating frontend state.
	•	Changing browser storage.

All access must be verified through backend authorization.

